From 980ddd112863b78cc1316b5136afa593f3c3f27c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jmaorr <fromjoshuaorr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:13:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Don't cache the max-content line when it refers to
 ::first-line styles

The inline content cache keeps the line built for the maximum intrinsic
width so a later layout that fits on one line can reuse it. Its runs hold
CheckedRefs to their styles. A ::first-line style lives in the renderer's
computed style and is destroyed by any style change on the renderer,
including repaint-only ones that leave this cache in place. The next
intrinsic width pass resets the cache and the dead style's CheckedRef
crashes (zombie), e.g. on the logged-in My Telstra header, whose flex
buttons style .mt-button__content:first-line.

Only cache the line when every run uses its box's own style (or its
parent's, for atomic inline-level boxes), which lives as long as the box.

Test: fast/inline/first-line-style-change-with-cached-max-content-line-crash.html

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ...cached-max-content-line-crash-expected.txt |  3 ++
 ...ge-with-cached-max-content-line-crash.html | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../inline/InlineFormattingContext.cpp        | 18 ++++++++--
 .../formattingContexts/inline/InlineLine.cpp  |  8 +++++
 .../formattingContexts/inline/InlineLineRun.h |  2 ++
 5 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 LayoutTests/fast/inline/first-line-style-change-with-cached-max-content-line-crash-expected.txt
